- What changes if array length is not multiple of four?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical low-level memory management with thread-safety using atomic bit ops on a compact bitmap. A beginner-friendly yet realistic task for systems work.

## Key Concepts

- Fixed-size block pools
- Bitmap-based tracking
- Atomic CAS and memory order
- Alignment and cache-friendly layout

## Code Example

```c
#include <stdatomic.h>
#include <stddef.h>

typedef struct {
  alignas(64) unsigned char arena[4096];
  atomic_uint64_t used;
} Pool;

void* allocate_block(Pool* p) {
  uint64_t oldv = atomic_load_explicit(&p->used, memory_order_relaxed);
  while (1) {
    uint64_t free = ~oldv;
    if (!free) return NULL;
    int idx = __builtin_ctzll(free);
    uint64_t want = oldv | (1ull << idx);
    if (atomic_compare_exchange_weak(&p->used, &oldv, want))
      return (void*)(p->arena + idx * 64);
  }
}

void free_block(Pool* p, void* ptr) {
  size_t idx = ((unsigned char*)ptr - p->arena) / 64;
  uint64_t mask = ~(1ull << idx);
  atomic_fetch_and_explicit(&p->used, mask, memory_order_release);
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect double-free? 
- How would you extend to multiple arenas or resizing?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests fundamentals of memory allocators, pointer arithmetic, alignment, and simple free-list management in a low-level setting. It also checks the ability to reason about initialization and fragmentation.

## Key Concepts
- Fixed-size allocator
- Free-list embedded pointers
- Heap initialization
- O(1) allocation/deallocation
- Fragmentation considerations with fixed-size pools

## Code Example
```c
#include <stdint.h>
#include <stddef.h>

#define HEAP_SIZE (64*1024)
#define BLOCK_SIZE 32
#define BLOCKS (HEAP_SIZE / BLOCK_SIZE)

static uint8_t heap[HEAP_SIZE];
static uint32_t free_head;

void init_heap(){
  free_head = 0;
  for(size_t i=0;i<BLOCKS;++i){
    uint32_t next = (i==BLOCKS-1) ? UINT32_MAX : (i+1);
    *((uint32_t*)(heap + i*BLOCK_SIZE)) = next;
  }
}

void* alloc_block(){
  if(free_head==UINT32_MAX) return NULL;
  uint32_t off = free_head;
  free_head = *((uint32_t*)(heap + off*BLOCK_SIZE));
  return (void*)(heap + off*BLOCK_SIZE);
}

void free_block(void* p){
  size_t off = ((uint8_t*)p - heap) / BLOCK_SIZE;
  *((uint32_t*)(heap + off*BLOCK_SIZE)) = free_head;
  free_head = off;
}
```

